   "exercise_v2": [
      {
         "question": "Is there only one calendar used worldwide?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "No",
         "additionalInfo": "Nowadays, different calendars are used around the world, with timekeeping linked to the Moon or to the Earth's orbit around the Sun, as we learned."
      },
      {
         "question": "Do the months of the Islamic and Gregorian calendars have at least 4 weeks?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "Yes",
         "additionalInfo": "Since the months have between 28 and 31 days, they all have at least four weeks, but they never reach exactly five weeks, as none of them has 35 days."
      },
      {
         "question": "Imagine that in some place on the planet, people decided the best way to organize the month would be in periods of 8 days, keeping 12 months with 30 days each. Will we also have, at a minimum, 4 periods of 8 days within a month?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "No",
         "additionalInfo": "Because we increased the length of the period used to organize the days within the month, the minimum number of periods decreases. This happens because 8 × 3 = 24, and the next multiple of 8, which is 32 (8 × 4 = 32), is greater than the 30-day month we defined.<br /><p><table class=\"htLongDivision\" style=\"width: 30%; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; font-weight: none; border-collapse: collapse;\"><tr><td>&nbsp; 30 </td><td style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid black; border-left: 2px solid black;\"> 8 </td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid black;\">- 24 </td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 6 </td><td> &nbsp; </td></tr> </table></p>"
      },
      {
         "question": "Imagine that in another place on the planet, people decided to organize the month into periods of 9 days, keeping 12 months with 30 days each. Will we also have, at a minimum, 3 periods of 9 days within a month?",
         "yesNoAnswer": "Yes",
         "additionalInfo": "Because we increased the length of the period used to organize the days within the month even more, but did not change the number of days in the month, we still have three periods, as in the previous exercise. This happens because 9 × 3 = 27, and the next multiple of 9, which is 36 (9 × 4 = 36), is greater than the 30-day month we defined.<br /><p><table class=\"htLongDivision\" style=\"width: 30%; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; font-weight: none; border-collapse: collapse;\"><tr><td>&nbsp; 30 </td><td style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid black; border-left: 2px solid black;\"> 9 </td></tr><tr><td style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid black;\">- 27 </td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 3 </td><td> &nbsp; </td></tr> </table></p>"
      }
   ],
